drills.explanation:
Start from the terminal handler and wrap it with each middleware from LAST to FIRST, so the first middleware ends up on the outside:

```csharp
var app = terminal;
for (var i = middleware.Count - 1; i >= 0; i--) app = middleware[i](app);
return app;
```

This is the same fold ASP.NET Core's `ApplicationBuilder.Build()` performs. Looping forwards instead would make the LAST registered middleware outermost and reverse the log.

